---@class azure.resourcehealth.AvailabilityStatusProperties
---@field availabilityState? azure.resourcehealth.AvailabilityStateValues Availability status of the resource. When it is null, this availabilityStatus object represents an availability impacting event
---@field title? string Title description of the availability status.
---@field summary? string Summary description of the availability status.
---@field detailedStatus? string Details of the availability status.
---@field reasonType? string When the resource's availabilityState is Unavailable, it describes where the health impacting event was originated. Examples are planned, unplanned, user initiated or an outage etc.
---@field context? string When an event is created, it can either be triggered by a customer or the platform of the resource and this field will illustrate that. This field is connected to the category field in this object.
---@field category? string When a context field is set to Platform, this field will reflect if the event was planned or unplanned. If the context field does not have a value of Platform, then this field will be ignored.
---@field articleId? string The Article Id
---@field rootCauseAttributionTime? string When the resource's availabilityState is Unavailable, it provides the Timestamp for when the health impacting event was received.
---@field healthEventType? string In case of an availability impacting event, it describes when the health impacting event was originated. Examples are Lifecycle, Downtime, Fault Analysis etc.
---@field healthEventCause? string In case of an availability impacting event, it describes where the health impacting event was originated. Examples are PlatformInitiated, UserInitiated etc.
---@field healthEventCategory? string In case of an availability impacting event, it describes the category of a PlatformInitiated health impacting event. Examples are Planned, Unplanned etc.
---@field healthEventId? string It is a unique Id that identifies the event
---@field resolutionETA? string When the resource's availabilityState is Unavailable and the reasonType is not User Initiated, it provides the date and time for when the issue is expected to be resolved.
---@field occuredTime? string Timestamp for when last change in health status occurred.
---@field reasonChronicity? azure.resourcehealth.ReasonChronicityTypes Chronicity of the availability transition.
---@field reportedTime? string Timestamp for when the health was last checked.
